To the southwest of the United States due to the remnants of Hurricane Rosa, there is heavy raining
Hurricane Rosa is predicted to move towards the cooler waters of the northern coast of Mexico and weaken.
However, in the coming days, Rosa will bring flooding in the north of Mexico and the southwest of the United States.
Rosa has been hurricane of the 1st category from 5:00 a.m. from 5:00 a.m., with a wind speed of 137 km/h and is located 620 kilometers southwest of Punte Eugenie in Mexico.
It is expected that Rosa will move north on Sunday.
Meanwhile, an area of low-pressure rises above the Pacific Ocean, moving east towards the west coast of the United States. Rosa will approach the Baja California peninsula on Monday as a tropical storm and will push high tropical humidity to the north to the southwest of the United States.
Rosa will bring up to 250 mm of rain in parts of Mexico on Monday.
Subsequently, tropical moisture, which will be mixed with the area of low air pressure, will create abundant precipitations in the wider south-western area in the coming days.
Locally, 25 to 100 mm of rain will cause dangerous flooding, debris deposition and the possibility of landslides in the desert.
Due to high tropical moisture, the amount of precipitation in some places will approach 50 to 75 mm per hour, mainly in parts of southern Nevada and Arizona.
In the south-western parts, mainly above the larger part of Arizona, 50 to 100 mm of precipitation is expected.
Floods are possible due to the rapid deterioration of the situation due to the diffuse nature of tropical rain.
It would be very reckless to walk into the desert when there is a risk of tropical rains.
