Celebrity Game of Thrones Kit Harington against toxic masculinity
Kit Harington is known for his wielding sword in the role of Jon Snow in HBO’s exciting medieval fantasy series Game of Thrones.
A 31-year-old actor who has sharply condemned the stereotype of a machistic hero says that due to the appearance of such roles on screens, young boys often feel that respect can only be deserved with resilience.
Kit told The Sunday Times Culture magazine that, in his opinion, something went wrong and wondered how to cope with the problem of toxic masculinity during the #Memore movement period.
Actor who recently married a 31-year-old teammate from Rose Leslie’s Game of Thrones has admitted that he has strong beliefs on the subject.
“Personally, I’m seriously wondering where we’ve made a mistake when it comes to masculinity,” he said.
“What did we teach men about the problems we’re dealing with?”
Kit believes that television is partly responsible for increasing toxic masculinity due to the display of very masculine characters.
He continued, “What is congenital and what is learned?
What are we taught on TV and on the streets that young boys feel that they have to choose exactly this particular side of masculinity?
I think it's one of the important questions of our time, how can we change it?
There seems to have been something wrong with young men.”
