In 1938, German officials were willing to carry out a coup against Hitler if the West rebelled against him and in Munich supported Czechoslovakia.
We didn’t make it possible for us to miss the opportunity to avoid the years of bowing that followed.
At such turning points, the course of history is changing, accelerating or hindering the relentless march of democracy.
The Americans are dealing with several such turning points right now.
